      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We, in this study, report a 72-year-old woman presenting with premature osteoarthritis of the spine, the hips, the knees and the shoulders symptomatic since the age of 50 years. The initial presentation of backache led to a mistaken diagnosis of ankylosing spondylitis. Subsequent manifestation of characteristic discoloration of her sclera and overnight dark urine led to the correct diagnosis of ochronosis."},
